            <ArticleTitle>Shoulder joint synovial chondromatosis presenting as multiple axillary masses: A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jcu.22555</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Synovial chondromatosis is a rare, benign, proliferative cartilaginous lesion arising from the synovial tissue, tenosynovium, or bursal lining. We describe the case of a patient who initially presented with multiple axillary masses. Breast ultrasound (US) was requested due to the concern of a breast tumor with axillary lymph node metastases. US study was helpful and provided adequate information to suggest the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
